   section 'Demographics':
      [[File:She ethnic townships in Jiangxi.png|thumb|150px|She ethnic townships in Jiangxi]]
      The population of Jiangxi according [[2020 Chinese census]] is 45.18 million. 99.73% of that is [[Han Chinese]], predominantly [[Gan-speaking people|Gan]] and [[Hakka people|Hakka]]. [[Ganzhou]], Jiangxi's largest city, has an especially large number of Hakka.
      Jiangxi and [[Henan]] both have the most unbalanced gender ratios of all Chinese provinces. Based on a 2009 ''[[British Medical Journal]]'' study, the ratio is over 140 boys for every 100 girls in the 1–4 age group.{{Update inline|date=December 2024}}
