   section 'Conquests by Northern Peoples':
      In 1127, the [[Jurchen people|Jurchens]], a people from the northeast, captured [[Kaifeng]] and [[Jingkang incident|took the Song emperor prisoner]]. In 1194, the Yellow River [[Changes in the course of the Yellow River|changed its course]], flowing southward 
      Due to heavy casualties and mass migration caused by warfare and flooding, the Ming court under the [[Hongwu Emperor|Hongwu]] reign organized large-scale, compulsory resettlement from [[Shanxi]] to Henan. In 1368, the prefectures of [[Weihui]] (衛輝), [[Zhangdef
      The wars of the late Ming and early [[Qing dynasty|Qing]] (circa 1630–1662) once again devastated Henan. During the [[Kangxi Emperor|Kangxi]] reign, the province's agricultural economy recovered, and it gradually regained its status as a major population cente
      On September 30, 1887, a major Yellow River dike breach occurred at Xiayun Shibao in Zhengzhou (present-day Shiqiao Village, [[Huayuankou, Henan|Huayuankou]] Town, Huiji District). The disaster claimed over two million lives (with estimates ranging from 930,00
   section 'Demographics':
