   section 'Unlisted ethnic groups':
      {{Main|Unrecognized ethnic groups in China}}
      {{More citations needed section|date=March 2024}}
      * Bajia ({{zhi|c=八甲人|p=Bājiǎrén}})
      * [[Macanese people]], mixed race Catholic [[Portuguese language|Portuguese]] speakers who lived in [[Macau]] since 16th century of various ethnic origins
      * {{Interlanguage link|Qago people|zh|木佬人}} (木佬人) – classified as Mulao
      During the [[Fifth National Population Census of the People's Republic of China]] held in 2000, 734,438 people on the mainland were recorded as belonging to "undistinguished ethnic groups"—of these, 97% resided in [[Guizhou]].{{Update inline|date=December 2024
